  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="87ea4671-e924-4106-8958-0fb20fd70e4b"><problem><para>
      <para>1. If y varies directly as \(x\) and \(y=14\), when \(x=3\). Find the equation that relates \(x\) and \(y\).</para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>y=\frac{14}{3}x</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(y=\frac{14}3x\). </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
